# Settings for the optional Itamos LLM router (itamos-llm-router.service).
# It sits in front of your llama-server instances (one per GPU) and sends each
# request to a GPU whose KV pool has room for it, counted in tokens; if none has
# room the request waits. The tools reach it through ITAMOS_SUMMARIZER_URL in
# /etc/itamos-mcp-tools/env (default http://127.0.0.1:8090).
#
# Format:  name|listen-port|backend@weight@pool,backend@weight@pool;name|port|...
#   weight = share of the work (a GPU twice as fast gets twice the weight)
#   pool   = the backend's KV pool in tokens (its -c, started with --kv-unified)
#
# Example: one MI50 (weight 4, pool 524288) and two smaller dies (weight 1, 262144):
#ROUTES=summarizer|8090|http://127.0.0.1:8190@4@524288,http://127.0.0.1:8092@1@262144,http://127.0.0.1:8094@1@262144;embedder|8091|http://127.0.0.1:8191@4,http://127.0.0.1:8093@1,http://127.0.0.1:8095@1
#
# Then: sudo systemctl enable --now itamos-llm-router
